annot connect while Phone Access is disabled. Paired-device records are kept, but mobile credentials are rejected until you enable this again.\",\"settings.components.settings.PhoneAccessCard.reachableServerUrl\":\"Discovered URL candidates\",\"settings.components.settings.PhoneAccessCard.refreshCandidates\":\"Refresh candidates\",\"settings.components.settings.PhoneAccessCard.manualPrivateNetworkUrl\":\"Phone-facing private network URL\",\"settings.components.settings.PhoneAccessCard.useManualUrl\":\"Use URL\",\"settings.components.settings.PhoneAccessCard.baseMobileContract\":\"Paste the /mobile URL here. AutoByteus stores the clean server base internally and creates the QR with /mobile.\",\"settings.components.settings.PhoneAccessCard.serveHttpsUrlHelp\":\"Recommended: paste a Tailscale Serve HTTPS /mobile URL. For home/local use, you may also paste a trusted private HTTP LAN/tailnet URL such as http://192.168.x.x:29695/mobile.\",\"settings.components.settings.PhoneAccessCard.candidatePlaceholder\":\"Choose a Tailscale HTTPS or trusted Local LAN candidate\",\"settings.components.settings.PhoneAccessCard.httpCandidateDiagnosticNote\":\"Tailscale Serve HTTPS remains recommended. Local LAN/private HTTP candidates can create QR codes after you acknowledge cleartext trusted-network use.\",\"settings.components.settings.PhoneAccessCard.remoteCandidateDiagnosticNote\":\"Discovered management candidates are diagnostic in remote-node windows. QR creation requires a manual phone-facing HTTPS or acknowledged trusted private HTTP URL mapped to this remote node.\",\"settings.components.settings.PhoneAccessCard.remoteAdvertisedUrlVerificationHelp\":\"Create QR will verify that this phone-facing URL reaches the same remote node as the desktop management URL before creating a pairing code.\",\"settings.components.settings.PhoneAccessCard.urlNeedsAttentionTitle\":\"URL needs attention\",\"settings.components.settings.PhoneAccessCard.privateHttpWarningTitle\":\"Trusted private HTTP\",\"settings.components.settings.PhoneAccessCard.privateHttpAcknowledgement\":\"I trust this private LAN/tailnet path and understand the QR and pairing traffic use cleartext HTTP. Do not use this on public or untrusted networks.\",\"settings.components.settings.PhoneAccessCard.createQrCode\":\"Create QR code\",\"settings.components.settings.PhoneAccessCard.revokeAllPhones\":\"Revoke all phones\",\"settings.components.settings.PhoneAccessCard.revokePhone\":\"Revoke\",\"settings.components.settings.PhoneAccessCard.pairedPhones\":\"Paired phones\",\"settings.components.settings.PhoneAccessCard.deviceViewsAria\":\"Paired phone views\",\"settings.components.settings.PhoneAccessCard.activeDevicesTab\":\"Active ({{count}})\",\"settings.components.settings.PhoneAccessCard.revokedDevicesTab\":\"Revoked / History ({{count}})\",\"settings.components.settings.PhoneAccessCard.pairedAt\":\"Paired {{date}}\",\"settings.components.settings.PhoneAccessCard.lastSeenAt\":\"Last seen {{date}}\",\"settings.components.settings.PhoneAccessCard.neverSeen\":\"never\",\"settings.components.settings.PhoneAccessCard.revokedAt\":\"Revoked {{date}}\",\"settings.components.settings.PhoneAccessCard.noActivePhonesPaired\":\"No active phones paired yet.\",\"settings.components.settings.PhoneAccessCard.noRevokedPhones\":\"No revoked phone history yet.\",\"settings.components.settings.PhoneAccessCard.pairingQr\":\"Pairing QR\",\"settings.components.settings.PhoneAccessCard.pairingQrDescription\":\"Scan or open this from the phone. It contains a short-lived one-time code, not the long-lived device credential.\",\"settings.components.settings.PhoneAccessCard.pairingQrAlt\":\"Phone Access pairing QR\",\"settings.components.settings.PhoneAccessCard.noActiveQrCode\":\"No active QR code.\",\"settings.components.settings.PhoneAccessCard.revokeAllConfirm\":\"Revoke every paired phone? Every phone must pair again.\",\"settings.components.settings.PhoneAccessCard.revokedCredentials\":\"Revoked {{count}} phone credential(s).\",\"settings.components.settings.PhoneSetupGuideCard.eyebrow\":\"Phone setup\",\"settings.components.settings.PhoneSetupGuideCard.title\":\"Set up private phone access\",\"settings.components.settings.PhoneSetupGuideCard.description\":\"Recommended: use Tailscale.app on this Mac to Serve AutoByteus at a stable private HTTPS MagicDNS URL. Trusted Local LAN HTTP is also available for home/local pairing.\",\"settings.components.settings.PhoneSetupGuideCard.targetUrlTitle\":\"Target mobile URL\",\"settings.components.settings.PhoneSetupGuideCard.targetUrlDescription\":\"After Serve is running, open or paste the mobile shell URL. AutoByteus will normalize it to the server base internally.\",\"settings.components.settings.PhoneSetupGuideCard.magicDnsGuidance\":\"Use the full MagicDNS hostname/FQDN shown by Tailscale, such as machine.tailnet.ts.net, for the HTTPS Serve URL. IPv4 and IPv6 are useful diagnostics, but they are not the preferred HTTPS certificate hostname.\",\"settings.components.settings.PhoneSetupGuideCard.installStepTitle\":\"1. Install and sign in to Tailscale.app on this Mac\",\"settings.components.settings.PhoneSetupGuideCard.macosCliNote\":\"Use Tailscale.app to sign in and confirm the full MagicDNS hostname/FQDN. AutoByteus only shows copyable commands; it does not run Tailscale or inspect local Tailscale status.\",\"settings.components.settings.PhoneSetupGuideCard.macosCommandsTitle\":\"2. Run Tailscale Serve on this Mac\",\"settings.components.settings.PhoneSetupGuideCard.macosCommandsDescription\":\"Run the background Serve command, then run Serve status and copy the HTTPS MagicDNS URL. Append /mobile before pasting it into Phone Access below.\",\"settings.components.settings.PhoneSetupGuideCard.platform.macos\":\"macOS\",\"settings.components.settings.PhoneSetupGuideCard.platformDescription.macos\":\"Install Tailscale.app, sign in, and use the direct app commands below for Serve.\",\"settings.components.settings.PhoneSetupGuideCard.commands.macosDirectServeForeground.title\":\"macOS app: Serve in foreground\",\"settings.components.settings.PhoneSetupGuideCard.commands.macosDirectServeForeground.description\":\"Starts Serve through the Tailscale.app executable while the command remains running.\",\"settings.components.settings.PhoneSetupGuideCard.commands.macosDirectServeBackground.title\":\"macOS app: Serve in background\",\"settings.components.settings.PhoneSetupGuideCard.commands.macosDirectServeBackground.description\":\"Starts Serve through the Tailscale.app executable and keeps it running after Terminal closes.\",\"settings.components.settings.PhoneSetupGuideCard.commands.macosDirectServeStatus.title\":\"macOS app: Inspect Serve status\",\"settings.components.settings.PhoneSetupGuideCard.commands.macosDirectServeStatus.description\":\"Prints the active Serve configuration through the Tailscale.app executable.\",\"settings.components.settings.PhoneSetupGuideCard.commands.macosDirectServeReset.title\":\"macOS app: Reset Serve\",\"settings.components.settings.PhoneSetupGuideCard.commands.macosDirectServeReset.description\":\"Clears the Serve configuration through the Tailscale.app executable if you need to start over.\",\"settings.components.settings.PhoneSetupGuideCard.copy\":\"Copy\",\"settings.components.settings.PhoneSetupGuideCard.copied\":\"Copied\",\"settings.components.settings.PhoneSetupGuideCard.copyCommandAria\":\"Copy {{command}} command\",\"settings.components.settings.PhoneSetupGuideCard.copyFailed\":\"Could not copy command: {{error}}\",\"settings.components.settings.PhoneSetupGuideCard.nextStep\":\"Copy the HTTPS MagicDNS URL from Serve status, append /mobile, paste it into the Phone Access URL field below, or choose a trusted Local LAN candidate below, then create the QR code.\",\"settings.components.settings.PhoneSetupGuideCard.funnelNote\":\"Use private tailnet Serve HTTPS for this setup. Public Funnel is not the recommended Phone Access path.\",\"settings.components.settings.DockerNodeStartGuideCard.eyebrow\":\"Docker node\",\"settings.components.settings.DockerNodeStartGuideCard.title\":\"Start Docker node\",\"settings.components.settings.DockerNodeStartGuideCard.description\":\"Install the Docker launcher once, then create a normal Docker node for local or trusted private-network access.\",\"settings.components.settings.DockerNodeStartGuideCard.installStepTitle\":\"1. Install launcher once\",\"settings.components.settings.DockerNodeStartGuideCard.directStepTitle\":\"2. Use direct commands\",\"settings.components.settings.DockerNodeStartGuideCard.directStepDescription\":\"After install, these commands run locally and do not download the launcher again.\",\"settings.components.settings.DockerNodeStartGuideCard.workspaceModel\":\"The launcher keeps private server state in Docker named volumes, publishes the server/browser ports, and creates host-visible workspace and shared-folder bind mounts.\",\"settings.components.settings.DockerNodeStartGuideCard.platform.macosLinux\":\"macOS / Linux\",\"settings.components.settings.DockerNodeStartGuideCard.platform.windowsPowerShell\":\"Windows PowerShell\",\"settings.components.settings.DockerNodeStartGuideCard.platform.installedCli\":\"Installed CLI\",\"settings.components.settings.DockerNodeStartGuideCard.commands.install.title\":\"Install autobyteus-docker\",\"settings.components.settings.DockerNodeStartGuideCard.commands.install.description\":\"Installs or replaces the local launcher and prints direct-path, current-shell PATH, and persistent profile/update or copy-paste setup guidance.\",\"settings.components.settings.DockerNodeStartGuideCard.commands.newContainer.title\":\"Create Docker node\",\"settings.components.settings.DockerNodeStartGuideCard.commands.newContainer.description\":\"Pulls the latest image and creates the next indexed Docker container, preferring friendly sequential host ports when available.\",\"settings.components.settings.DockerNodeStartGuideCard.commands.upgradeAll.title\":\"Upgrade all Docker nodes\",\"settings.components.settings.DockerNodeStartGuideCard.commands.upgradeAll.description\":\"Recreates all managed containers with each node's saved image ref while keeping named volumes.\",\"settings.components.settings.DockerNodeStartGuideCard.commands.destroyAll.title\":\"Destroy all Docker nodes\",\"settings.components.settings.DockerNodeStartGuideCard.commands.destroyAll.description\":\"Removes all managed containers and unused old images while keeping named volumes.\",\"settings.components.settings.DockerNodeStartGuideCard.commands.destroyNode.title\":\"Destroy one Docker node\",\"settings.components.settings.DockerNodeStartGuideCard.commands.destroyNode.description\":\"Run autobyteus-docker status first, then replace <node-name> with the exact managed node name. This removes only that node's container and launcher state while keeping named volumes and host workspaces; the freed indexed slot can be reused by the next new-container invocation.\",\"settings.components.settings.DockerNodeStartGuideCard.commands.reset.title\":\"Reset Docker nodes\",\"settings.components.settings.DockerNodeStartGuideCard.commands.reset.description\":\"Destroys all managed containers, keeps volumes, then creates a fresh autobyteus-server-0.\",\"settings.components.settings.DockerNodeStartGuideCard.commands.workspacePaths.title\":\"Show workspace paths\",\"settings.components.settings.DockerNodeStartGuideCard.commands.workspacePaths.description\":\"Prints the host folders backing /home/autobyteus/workspace and /home/autobyteus/shared for all managed nodes by default.\",\"settings.components.settings.DockerNodeStartGuideCard.commands.workspaceApplyAll.title\":\"Apply shared workspace to all nodes\",\"settings.components.settings.DockerNodeStartGuideCard.commands.workspaceApplyAll.description\":\"Safely recreates managed containers with the new bind mounts while keeping existing named volumes.\",\"settings.components.settings.DockerNodeStartGuideCard.commands.storage.title\":\"Inspect Docker storage\",\"settings.components.settings.DockerNodeStartGuideCard.commands.storage.description\":\"Shows private named volumes, host bind mounts, and launcher state for all managed nodes by default.\",\"settings.components.settings.DockerNodeStartGuideCard.commands.urls.title\":\"Show Docker node URLs\",\"settings.components.settings.DockerNodeStartGuideCard.commands.urls.description\":\"Prints Backend, noVNC, VNC, and debug URLs for all managed nodes by default.\",\"settings.components.settings.DockerNodeStartGuideCard.commands.status.title\":\"Show Docker node status\",\"settings.components.settings.DockerNodeStartGuideCard.commands.status.description\":\"Lists managed nodes and their current Docker status.\",\"settings.components.settings.DockerNodeStartGuideCard.commands.logs.title\":\"Show Docker node logs\",\"settings.components.settings.DockerNodeStartGuideCard.commands.logs.description\":\"Prints recent logs for autobyteus-server-0 unless you pass another node name.\",\"settings.components.settings.DockerNodeStartGuideCard.commands.stop.title\":\"Stop Docker node\",\"settings.components.settings.DockerNodeStartGuideCard.commands.stop.description\":\"Stops autobyteus-server-0 by default without deleting named volumes.\",\"settings.components.settings.DockerNodeStartGuideCard.copy\":\"Copy\",\"settings.components.settings.DockerNodeStartGuideCard.copied\":\"Copied\",\"settings.components.settings.DockerNodeStartGuideCard.copyCommandAria\":\"Copy {{command}} command\",\"settings.components.settings.DockerNodeStartGuideCard.copyFailed\":\"Could not copy command: {{error}}\",\"settings.components.settings.DockerNodeStartGuideCard.nextStep\":\"After new-container prints Backend, paste that URL into Add Remote Node and open the Docker node window over your trusted private network. For Phone Access, create the QR there with a verified phone-facing HTTPS or acknowledged trusted private HTTP /mobile URL that the phone can reach.\"},BN={\"settings.components.settings.ProviderAPIKeyManager.manage_provider_keys_and_reload_available\":\"Manage provider keys and provider-specific model discovery\",\"settings.components.settings.ProviderAPIKeyManager.reloading_and_discovering_models\":\"Reloading and discovering models...\",\"settings.components.settings.ProviderAPIKeyManager.loading_available_models\":\"Loading available models...\",\"settings.components.settings.ProviderAPIKeyManager.loading_credentials\":\"Loading provider credentials...\",\"settings.components.settings.ProviderAPIKeyManager.credentials_unavailable\":\"Provider credentials unavailable\",\"settings.components.settings.ProviderAPIKeyManager.models\":\"Models\",\"settings.components.settings.ProviderAPIKeyManager.loading_models\":\"Loading models…\",\"settings.components.settings.ProviderAPIKeyManager.refreshing_models\":\"Refreshing models…\",\"settings.components.settings.ProviderAPIKeyManager.models_unavailable\":\"Models unavailable\",\"settings.components.settings.ProviderAPIKeyManager.models_unavailable_description\":\"Could not load models. Your provider credentials remain available.\",\"settings.components.settings.ProviderAPIKeyManager.some_model_sources_unavailable\":\"Some model sources were unavailable\",\"settings.components.settings.ProviderAPIKeyManager.showing_last_known_models\":\"Could not refresh models. Showing last known models.\",\"settings.components.settings.ProviderAPIKeyManager.retry\":\"Retry\",\"settings.components.settings.ProviderAPIKeyManager.model_count_loading\":\"Model count loading\",\"settings.components.settings.ProviderAPIKeyManager.video_models\":\"Video Models\",\"settings.components.settings.ProviderAPIKeyManager.no_models_available\":\"No models available. Configure at least one provider API key to see available models.\",\"settings.components.settings.ProviderAPIKeyManager.providers\":\"Providers\",\"settings.components.settings.ProviderAPIKeyManager.configured\":\"Configured\",\"sett